---
/*
  The UK aesthetics search teardown.

  Rebuilt from docs/uk-aesthetics-teardown-source.html, which is now a content
  and chart reference rather than a template. Its CSS was deliberately left
  behind: on AnalysisLayout the page inherits this site's light and dark
  themes, the site nav and footer, and the Report structured data that makes a
  claim citable rather than merely readable.

  Why it lives on this domain at all. Four of the five cold email sequences
  link this piece on day 9. The only published copy used to sit on a claude.ai
  artifact URL, which built authority for someone else's domain and looked odd
  enough to cost trust at exactly the wrong moment.

  Two things about this file that are load-bearing, not incidental:

  1. Every figure keeps its "Semrush UK estimates" label and section 06 keeps
     the full method paragraph. The restraint is why the piece works on a
     sceptical reader. Do not remove a caveat to make a claim sound stronger,
     and do not add a call to action that turns it into an advert.
  2. It ends with five checks anyone can run in ten minutes, and no pitch.
     Keep that ending.

  The source's hover crosshair was dropped in this port. It was decoration,
  it was the only client-side script on the page, and the hot-zone rectangles
  that drove it were about half the weight of each chart.

  This route is a static .astro file, and Astro matches static segments ahead
  of dynamic ones, so blog/[slug].astro never serves it. A blogPosts document
  with this exact slug exists purely to feed the blog index and the RSS feed,
  which are driven by the CMS collection and cannot see a file. If you change
  one, change the other: scripts/check-blog-routes.mjs fails the build if they
  drift apart.
*/
import AnalysisLayout from "../../layouts/AnalysisLayout.astro";
import SectionHead from "../../components/analysis/SectionHead.astro";
import StatTiles from "../../components/analysis/StatTiles.astro";
import Figure from "../../components/analysis/Figure.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/analysis/Callout.astro";

const tiles = [
    {
        who: "sk:n Clinics",
        big: "−33%",
        sub: "Britain's largest chain. Down from about 199,000 monthly visits to 134,000 since its late-2024 peak.",
        series: 1 as const,
    },
    {
        who: "EF MEDISPA",
        big: "−28%",
        sub: "From roughly 10,600 monthly visits to 7,700. A slower bleed, same direction.",
        series: 2 as const,
    },
    {
        who: "Dr Leah",
        big: "+75%",
        sub: "From about 22,000 monthly visits to 38,700, and now ahead of where it was on far fewer pages.",
        series: 3 as const,
    },
];
---

